source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-24
observed: Each cell is its own line domain, so the pair in every cell is that cell's last run and Jira breaks in both. A GFM cell carries no hard break, so jiro keeps the whole row as raw Jira Markup rather than writing a table it could not read back.
-- input.jira --
||h1||h2||
|a\\b|c\\d|
-- rendered.html --
<div class='table-wrap'>
<table class='confluenceTable'><tbody>
<tr>
<th class='confluenceTh'>h1</th>
<th class='confluenceTh'>h2</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class='confluenceTd'>a<br class="atl-forced-newline" />b</td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>c<br class="atl-forced-newline" />d</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
</div>
-- want.md --
:::table
||h1||h2||
|a\\b|c\\d|
:::
-- warnings.json --
[]
